IMPORT prelude

-- Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) -- donation of tissue after death (Part 3: ss 22, 23, 24(2)), with the definitions
-- it uses in s 3(1) (child; next of kin; senior available next of kin), and the adult living donor's consent to the removal of
-- nonregenerative tissue (ss 9, 12(2), 16).
--
-- Edition: compilation as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49110.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 49110,
-- retrieved 7 September 2026). The deposit's compilation table runs to the Therapeutic Goods Law Application Act 2024 Pt. 8
-- Div. 1 (No. 19 of 2024, in operation 30 August 2024); the last reprint it lists is Reprint 3 as at 19 May 2017. The Assisted
-- Reproductive Technology and Surrogacy Act 2025 Pt. 16 is listed as uncommenced and is not reflected.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. au/wa:REQ-0009 in ../../../requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 4 times by the Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave lives: chloe c026 (2021-03-20, registers on the Australian Organ Donor Register at 18 -- "Is donation opt-in
-- or presumed?"), daniel d021 (2014-04-09, registers at 18), jake k097 (2079-04-18, dies at 72, on the Register since 2047,
-- kidneys donated -- "Is consent presumed or given; who may object?") and daniel d092 (2078-10-21, dies at 82, on the Register,
-- the family confirms -- "Whose consent governs donation?"). Every one cites s 22. SCOPED to s 22 and what is needed to answer
-- those questions: the s 3(1) definitions of child and senior available next of kin, the coroner's consent for a reportable
-- death (s 23), the brain-death declaration for a body on artificial respiration (s 24(2)), and -- because the lives turn 18 --
-- the age-18 condition on a living donor's consent (ss 9, 12(2), 16).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: designated officers and delegation (ss 4, 5, 5A) beyond the officer's power itself; regenerative tissue, children
-- and blood (ss 8, 10-15, 17-21); who may remove tissue under an authority (s 24(1), (1A), 24A); postmortem examinations
-- (Part 4); trading in tissue (Part 5); embryonic stem cell lines (Part 6); liability, codes of practice, offences and
-- disclosure (Part 7). The Australian Organ Donor Register is a Commonwealth register: THE DEPOSITED TEXT DOES NOT MENTION IT.
-- Treating a registration as the deceased's "expressed ... wish for, or consent to" removal (s 22(2)(a)) is an INFERENCE.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC USE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 -- donation`

§§ `3(1) -- child, next of kin, senior available next of kin`

-- s 3(1): "child means a person who has not attained the age of 18 years".
-- "senior available next of kin -- (a) in relation to a child, means the first in order of priority of the following persons
-- who is available at the time -- (i) if the child has both a spouse, and a de facto partner who has attained the age of 18
-- years, the spouse or de facto partner with whom the child is living as a spouse or de facto partner; (ia) the spouse, or de
-- facto partner who has attained the age of 18 years, of the child; (ii) a parent of the child; (iii) a brother or sister, who
-- has attained the age of 18 years, of the child; (iv) a guardian of the child; and (b) in relation to a person other than a
-- child ... (i) [as above]; (ia) [as above]; (ii) a son or daughter, who has attained the age of 18 years, of the person; (iii) a
-- parent of the person; (iv) a brother or sister, who has attained the age of 18 years, of the person".
-- A former spouse, a grandchild, a friend and (for an adult) a guardian appear nowhere in the list.
DECLARE Kinship IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `de facto partner`
    `former spouse`
    `son or daughter`
    `parent`
    `brother or sister`
    `guardian`
    `another relative or friend`

-- `consents to the removal` means consent to the removal of THIS tissue for THIS purpose (s 22(3)(b) restricts the authority
-- "both as to the tissue which may be removed and as to the purpose or use of the tissue").
DECLARE Relative HAS
    `kinship` IS A Kinship
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `is available at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with the deceased as a spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consents to the removal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `objects to the removal` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Deceased HAS
    `age at death` IS A NUMBER
    `died in a hospital or was brought into one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `expressed a wish for or consented to removal in life, not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the removal is within the terms of that wish or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer has reason to believe the deceased objected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the death is or may be a reportable death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the coroner consented or directed that consent is not required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `respiration and circulation are maintained by artificial means` IS A BOOLEAN
    `two qualifying practitioners declared brain function irreversibly ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relatives` IS A LIST OF Relative

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deceased was a child` d IF d's `age at death` LESS THAN 18

GIVEN r IS A Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a spouse or adult de facto partner` r IF
        r's `kinship` EQUALS `spouse`
    OR  (r's `kinship` EQUALS `de facto partner` AND r's `age` AT LEAST 18)

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a spouse is among` rs MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r's `kinship` EQUALS `spouse` OR `a spouse is among` rest

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an adult de facto partner is among` rs MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (r's `kinship` EQUALS `de facto partner` AND r's `age` AT LEAST 18)
        OR  `an adult de facto partner is among` rest

-- Paragraph (i): "if the person HAS both a spouse, and a de facto partner who has attained the age of 18 years". Read as all
-- the relatives, available or not.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has both a spouse and an adult de facto partner` d IF
    `a spouse is among` (d's `relatives`) AND `an adult de facto partner is among` (d's `relatives`)

-- The subparagraph a relative falls in, numbered 1 to 5 in the order (i), (ia), (ii), (iii), (iv); 0 if in none.
GIVEN r IS A Relative, d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the priority of the relative` r d MEANS
    IF `is a spouse or adult de facto partner` r
    THEN IF `has both a spouse and an adult de facto partner` d AND r's `lives with the deceased as a spouse or de facto partner`
         THEN 1
         ELSE 2
    ELSE IF `the deceased was a child` d
         THEN CONSIDER r's `kinship`
              WHEN `parent` THEN 3
              WHEN `brother or sister` THEN IF r's `age` AT LEAST 18 THEN 4 ELSE 0
              WHEN `guardian` THEN 5
              OTHERWISE 0
         ELSE CONSIDER r's `kinship`
              WHEN `son or daughter` THEN IF r's `age` AT LEAST 18 THEN 3 ELSE 0
              WHEN `parent` THEN 4
              WHEN `brother or sister` THEN IF r's `age` AT LEAST 18 THEN 5 ELSE 0
              OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher priority` a b MEANS
    IF a EQUALS 0 THEN b
    ELSE IF b EQUALS 0 THEN a
         ELSE IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
      d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the highest priority available among` rs d MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `the higher priority`
            (IF r's `is available at the time` THEN `the priority of the relative` r d ELSE 0)
            (`the highest priority available among` rest d)

-- "the first in order of priority ... who is available at the time"; 0 means there is no senior available next of kin.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the senior available next of kin's priority` d MEANS `the highest priority available among` (d's `relatives`) d

GIVEN r IS A Relative, d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a senior available next of kin` r d IF
        r's `is available at the time`
    AND `the senior available next of kin's priority` d GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the priority of the relative` r d EQUALS `the senior available next of kin's priority` d

§§ `22(2)(b), (5) -- the senior available next of kin consents`

-- s 22(5): "Where there are 2 or more persons having a description referred to in a subparagraph of paragraph (a) or (b) of the
-- definition of 'senior available next of kin' in section 3, an objection by any one of those persons has effect for the purposes
-- of this section notwithstanding any indication to the contrary by the other or any other of those persons."
-- Read as: one objection within the senior description defeats the others' consent. An objection by a person of a LOWER
-- description has no effect, and (5) does not ask whether the objector is "available" (both readings, not ruled by the text).
GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
      d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a senior available next of kin among` rs `consents` d MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (`is a senior available next of kin` r d AND r's `consents to the removal`)
        OR  `a senior available next of kin among` rest `consents` d

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
      d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`someone of the senior description among` rs `objects` d MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (    `the senior available next of kin's priority` d GREATER THAN 0
             AND `the priority of the relative` r d EQUALS `the senior available next of kin's priority` d
             AND r's `objects to the removal`)
        OR  `someone of the senior description among` rest `objects` d

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the senior available next of kin consents` d IF
        `a senior available next of kin among` (d's `relatives`) `consents` d
    AND (NOT `someone of the senior description among` (d's `relatives`) `objects` d)

§§ `22(1), (2), (3) -- the designated officer may authorise removal`

-- s 22(1): a designated officer for a hospital may authorise removal "from the body of a person who has died in hospital or whose
-- dead body has been brought into the hospital" for transplantation, other therapeutic, medical or scientific purposes, or
-- training, education or quality assurance.
-- (2)(a): "where, after making inquiries, the designated officer is satisfied that the deceased person during the person's lifetime
-- expressed the wish for, or consented to, the removal after death of tissue ... and had not withdrawn the wish or revoked the
-- consent"; or
-- (2)(b): "where, after making inquiries, the designated officer has no reason to believe that the deceased person had expressed an
-- objection ... and the designated officer is satisfied that the senior available next of kin consents".
-- (3): the authority is restricted (a) by "the expressed terms of the wishes or consent of the deceased person"; (b) by "the consent
-- of the senior available next of kin", "both as to the tissue which may be removed and as to the purpose or use".
--
-- There is no third limb. Silence from the deceased and no consent from the senior available next of kin is no authority:
-- donation is not presumed. Paragraph (a) says nothing about the family, so -- on the text -- a family objection does not defeat
-- the deceased's own expressed wish. Part 3 sets no minimum age for that wish.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph (a) is met` d IF
        d's `died in a hospital or was brought into one`
    AND d's `expressed a wish for or consented to removal in life, not withdrawn`
    AND d's `the removal is within the terms of that wish or consent`

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph (b) is met` d IF
        d's `died in a hospital or was brought into one`
    AND (NOT d's `the officer has reason to believe the deceased objected`)
    AND `the senior available next of kin consents` d

§§ `23 -- the coroner's consent for a reportable death`

-- s 23(1): "If the designated officer for a hospital has reason to believe that the death of a person is or may be a reportable
-- death, the designated officer must not, under and in accordance with section 22, authorise the removal of tissue ... unless the
-- coroner has given consent to the removal." (2): a coroner may direct, before or after death, that consent is not required.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 23 bars the authority` d IF
        d's `the death is or may be a reportable death`
    AND (NOT d's `the coroner consented or directed that consent is not required`)

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the designated officer may authorise the removal` d IF
        (`paragraph (a) is met` d OR `paragraph (b) is met` d)
    AND (NOT `section 23 bars the authority` d)

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `the deceased's own wish or consent under s 22(2)(a)`
    `the senior available next of kin's consent under s 22(2)(b)`
    `no authority`

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A Ground
`the ground for the authority` d MEANS
    IF `section 23 bars the authority` d THEN `no authority`
    ELSE IF `paragraph (a) is met` d THEN `the deceased's own wish or consent under s 22(2)(a)`
         ELSE IF `paragraph (b) is met` d THEN `the senior available next of kin's consent under s 22(2)(b)`
              ELSE `no authority`

§§ `22(4) -- next of kin consent while the person is unconscious`

-- s 22(4): the senior available next of kin may make known, "at any time when the person is unconscious before death", consent to
-- removal after death, "but the designated officer must not act on such an indication if the person recovers consciousness".
GIVEN `the person recovered consciousness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may act on the indication given during unconsciousness` IF NOT `the person recovered consciousness`

§§ `24(2) -- a body on artificial respiration and circulation`

-- s 24(2): "Where the respiration and the circulation of the blood of a person are being maintained by artificial means, tissue must
-- not be removed ... unless 2 medical practitioners (each of whom has carried out a clinical examination of the person, each of whom
-- has been for a period of not less than 5 years a medical practitioner and one of whom holds specialist qualifications in general
-- medicine, neurology or neurosurgery or has such other qualifications as are accepted by the Chief Health Officer) have declared
-- that irreversible cessation of all function of the brain of the person has occurred." The qualifications are one input here.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tissue may be removed under the authority` d IF
        `the designated officer may authorise the removal` d
    AND (    (NOT d's `respiration and circulation are maintained by artificial means`)
         OR  d's `two qualifying practitioners declared brain function irreversibly ceased`)

§§ `9, 12(2), 16 -- a living adult donating nonregenerative tissue`

-- s 9(1): a person who "(a) has attained the age of 18 years; and (b) is of sound mind; and (c) is in the light of medical advice
-- furnished to the person prepared to do so, may, by writing signed by the person otherwise than in the presence of any member of
-- the person's family or any of the person's friends, consent to the removal, after the expiration of a period of 24 hours from the
-- time at which the consent is signed, ... of nonregenerative tissue ... for the purpose of the transplantation of the tissue to the
-- body of another living person". (2): revocable, orally or in writing, before removal.
-- s 12(2): "It is not lawful to remove nonregenerative tissue from the body of a living child for the purpose of the transplantation".
-- s 16: the consent is sufficient authority, unless revoked, to remove the tissue "after the expiration of a period of 24 hours".
-- Whether removal at exactly 24 hours is "after the expiration" is not asserted.
GIVEN `the donor's age` IS A NUMBER, `of sound mind` IS A BOOLEAN, `prepared in the light of medical advice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `signed in writing away from family and friends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may consent to living donation of nonregenerative tissue` IF
        `the donor's age` AT LEAST 18
    AND `of sound mind`
    AND `prepared in the light of medical advice`
    AND `signed in writing away from family and friends`

GIVEN `hours since the consent was signed` IS A NUMBER, `the consent was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent authorises removal now` IF
        `hours since the consent was signed` AT LEAST 24
    AND (NOT `the consent was revoked`)
